62,"total":16.9},"snow_normal":51.5},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, 1 daily record low","records":"Battle Creek has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"Battle Creek's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 39\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>39\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 48\u00b0F, and the record is 71\u00b0F (1989). The low of <strong>28\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Battle Creek has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Battle Creek's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Battle Creek has set <strong class=\"sig\">28 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 74 that chance alone would give, and <strong>72 record highs</strong>, close to the 74 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (52). Battle Creek's all-time high is 104\u00b0F, on July 14, 1936.","t_chg":"Battle Creek's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 130 complete years: Battle Creek's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.09 to +0.24), about +2.2\u00b0F since 1895. Battle Creek's average high shows no clear change: +0.07\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.14) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. July and August highs have edged down across the full record; the 1930s summers were the hottest in it.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months; July and August fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Battle Creek's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.02 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 32.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1985 (47.67 in); the driest, 2005 (21.24 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}